{'problem_index': 114, 'code': '### Step 1: Understand the Problem\n\nWe are given two natural numbers \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) such that:\n1. \\( 1 \\leq a \\leq 9 \\)\n2. \\( b \\leq 9 \\)\n3. \\( 10a + b = 2(a + b) \\)\n\nWe need to find the value of \\( 10a + b \\).\n\n### Step 2: Simplify the Equation\n\nFirst, expand the right-hand side of the equation:\n\\[ 10a + b = 2a + 2b \\]\n\nNext, subtract \\( 2a + 2b \\) from both sides to bring all terms to one side:\n\\[ 10a + b - 2a - 2b = 0 \\]\n\\[ 8a - b = 0 \\]\n\\[ b = 8a \\]\n\n### Step 3: Apply the Constraints\n\nFrom the equation \\( b = 8a \\), we can substitute \\( b \\) in terms of \\( a \\). Since \\( b \\leq 9 \\), we have:\n\\[ 8a \\leq 9 \\]\n\\[ a \\leq \\frac{9}{8} \\]\n\\[ a \\leq 1.125 \\]\n\nBut since \\( a \\) is a natural number and \\( a \\geq 1 \\), the only possible value for \\( a \\) is \\( a = 1 \\).\n\n### Step 4: Find \\( b \\)\n\nSubstitute \\( a = 1 \\) into \\( b = 8a \\):\n\\[ b = 8 \\times 1 = 8 \\]\n\n### Step 5: Verify the Solution\n\nCheck if \\( a = 1 \\) and \\( b = 8 \\) satisfy the original equation:\n\\[ 10a + b = 10 \\times 1 + 8 = 18 \\]\n\\[ 2(a + b) = 2(1 + 8) = 2 \\times 9 = 18 \\]\nBoth sides are equal, so the solution is correct.\n\n### Step 6: Conclusion\n\nThe value of \\( 10a + b \\) is \\( 18 \\).\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[ \\boxed{18} \\]', 'error': 'failed after too many retries'}
