{'problem_index': 196, 'code': '### Step 1: Substitute \\( c = i \\) into the equations\n\nGiven:\n1. \\( a + b = 2c \\)\n2. \\( c = i \\)\n\nSubstitute \\( c = i \\) into the first equation:\n\\[ a + b = 2i \\]\n\n### Step 2: Express \\( a \\) in terms of \\( b \\)\n\nFrom \\( a + b = 2i \\), we can express \\( a \\) as:\n\\[ a = 2i - b \\]\n\n### Step 3: Compute \\( a \\cdot c + b \\cdot c \\)\n\nSubstitute \\( a = 2i - b \\) and \\( c = i \\) into \\( a \\cdot c + b \\cdot c \\):\n\\[\na \\cdot c + b \\cdot c = (2i - b) \\cdot i + b \\cdot i\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2i \\cdot i - b \\cdot i + b \\cdot i\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2i^2 - b \\cdot i + b \\cdot i\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2(-1) - b \\cdot i + b \\cdot i \\quad \\text{(since \\( i^2 = -1 \\))}\n\\]\n\\[\n= -2 - b \\cdot i + b \\cdot i\n\\]\n\\[\n= -2\n\\]\n\nThus, \\( a \\cdot c + b \\cdot c = -2 \\).\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-2}\n\\]', 'error': 'failed after too many retries'}
