{'problem_index': 206, 'code': '### Final Lean4 Code\n\ntheorem algebra_2varlineareq_xpeeq7_2xpeeq3_eeq11_xeqn4 (x e : ℂ) (h₀ : x + e = 7)\n  (h₁ : 2 * x + e = 3) : e = 11 ∧ x = -4 := by\n  have h₂ : x = -4 := by\n    have h₃ : x = -4 := by\n      linear_combination h₁ - h₀\n    exact h₃\n  have h₃ : e = 11 := by\n    have h₄ : e = 11 := by\n      linear_combination h₀ - x\n    exact h₄\n  exact ⟨h₃, h₂⟩', 'error': 'failed after too many retries'}
{'problem_index': 207, 'code': "### Step 1: Understanding the Problem\n\nWe need to find a function \\( f: \\mathbb{N} \\to \\mathbb{N} \\) such that:\n1. \\( f(1) = 2 \\),\n2. For all \\( n \\in \\mathbb{N} \\), \\( f(f(n)) = f(n) + n \\),\n3. For all \\( n \\in \\mathbb{N} \\), \\( f(n) < f(n + 1) \\).\n\n### Step 2: Guessing the Form of \\( f \\)\n\nWe can try to find a pattern or a simple form for \\( f \\). Let's consider the condition \\( f(f(n)) = f(n) + n \\).\n\nSuppose \\( f \\) is linear, i.e., \\( f(n) = a n + b \\). Then:\n\\[ f(f(n)) = a (a n + b) + b = a^2 n + a b + b \\]\n\\[ f(n) + n = a n + b + n = a n + n + b \\]\n\nFor these to be equal:\n\\[ a^2 n + a b + b = a n + n + b \\]\n\\[ a^2 n + a b = a n + n \\]\n\\[ a^2 n - a n - n + a b = 0 \\]\n\\[ n (a^2 - a - 1) + a b = 0 \\]\n\nThis must hold for all \\( n \\). The only way this can happen is if the coefficients of \\( n \\) and the constant term are zero:\n1. \\( a^2 - a - 1 = 0 \\),\n2. \\( a b = 0 \\).\n\nThe quadratic equation \\( a^2 - a - 1 = 0 \\) has solutions:\n\\[ a = \\frac{1 \\pm \\sqrt{1 + 4}}{2} = \\frac{1 \\pm \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\]\n\nSince \\( a \\) must be a natural number, the only possible value is \\( a = 1 \\) (since \\( \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\approx 1.618 \\) is not a natural number, and \\( \\frac{1 - \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\approx -0", 'error': 'failed after too many retries'}
{'problem_index': 208, 'code': 'theorem numbertheory_prmdvsneqnsqmodpeq0 (n : ℤ) (p : ℕ) (h₀ : Nat.Prime p) :\n  ↑p ∣ n ↔ n ^ 2 % ↑p = 0 := by\n  norm_cast\n  rw [Int.coe_nat_dvd_left]\n  simp [← Int.coe_nat_dvd, pow_two]\n  <;>\n    simp_all [Int.emod_eq_of_lt]\n  <;>\n    omega\n  <;>\n    aesop\n  <;>\n    omega\n  <;>\n    aesop\n  <;>\n    omega\n  <;>\n    aesop', 'error': 'failed after too many retries'}
{'problem_index': 209, 'code': 'theorem imo_1964_p1_1 (n : ℕ) (h₀ : 7 ∣ 2 ^ n - 1) : 3 ∣ n := by\n  rw [Nat.dvd_iff_mod_eq_zero] at h₀ ⊢\n  contrapose! h₀\n  rw [← Nat.mod_add_div n 3]\n  have h₁ : n % 3 = 1 ∨ n % 3 = 2 := by omega\n  cases h₁ with\n  | inl h₁ =>\n    rw [h₁]\n    norm_num\n    induction n / 3 with\n    | zero => norm_num\n    | succ k ih =>\n      simp [pow_add, pow_mul, Nat.mul_mod, Nat.pow_mod, Nat.add_mod] at ih ⊢\n      omega\n  | inr h₁ =>\n    rw [h₁]\n    norm_num\n    induction n / 3 with\n    | zero => norm_num\n    | succ k ih =>\n      simp [pow_add, pow_mul, Nat.mul_mod, Nat.pow_mod, Nat.add_mod] at ih ⊢\n      omega', 'result': 'no bug, can double check'}
{'problem_index': 210, 'code': 'theorem imo_1990_p3 (n : ℕ) (h₀ : 2 ≤ n) (h₁ : n ^ 2 ∣ 2 ^ n + 1) : n = 3 := by\n  have h₂ : n ≤ 18 := by\n    have h₃ : n ≤ 18 := by\n      by_contra! h\n      have h₄ : n ≥ 19 := by linarith\n      have h₅ : n ^ 2 ∣ 2 ^ n + 1 := h₁\n      have h₆ : 2 ^ n % n ^ 2 = (2 ^ n + 1) % n ^ 2 := by\n        rw [← Nat.mod_add_div (2 ^ n) (n ^ 2)]\n        simp_all [Nat.dvd_iff_mod_eq_zero]\n        <;> omega\n      have h₇ : n ≥ 19 := by linarith\n      have h₈ : 2 ^ n % n ^ 2 = (2 ^ n + 1) % n ^ 2 := by\n        rw [← Nat.mod_add_div (2 ^ n) (n ^ 2)]\n        simp_all [Nat.dvd_iff_mod_eq_zero]\n        <;> omega\n      have h₉ : n ≤ 18 := by\n        by_contra! h₁₀\n        have h₁₁ : n ≥ 19 := by linarith\n        have h₁₂ : 2 ^ n % n ^ 2 = (2 ^ n + 1) % n ^ 2 := by\n          rw [← Nat.mod_add_div (2 ^ n) (n ^ 2)]\n          simp_all [Nat.dvd_iff_mod_eq_zero]\n          <;> omega\n        have h₁₃ : n ≤ 18 := by\n          interval_cases n <;> norm_num [Nat.pow_succ, Nat.mul_mod, Nat.add_mod] at h₁₂ <;> omega\n        linarith\n      linarith\n    linarith', 'error': 'failed after too many retries'}
